(
    title: "Air-Sea Battle",
    developer: Some("Larry Kaplan"),
    description: Some("A cartridge of 27 numbered target-shooting games, chosen with the console\'s Game Select switch rather than an on-screen menu. Depending on the number you pick, you fire at aircraft crossing overhead, ships from a submarine below, rabbits, ducks and clowns in a shooting gallery, or Polaris-style bombing runs; the mode fixes whether the gun\'s angle or its speed is under your control, and some pit two players or a player against the computer. A round ends at a short time limit or when someone reaches 99 points."),
